   "author": "Hollowmere team",
   "population": "hunters",
   "story": "Ray Hollis sold every rifle off his wall the first week, to men heading up into the hills with their families. When the Cordon came round collecting guns he pulled the grille down, bolted the door and moved what was left into the vault room. His nephew Danny came in through the alley with a bite on his forearm and Ray did what he'd promised Danny's mother: he locked the boy in the vault with a lamp and a radio, to sit it out. Then he went down to the range with the key on its lanyard, the bottle and the .38, and he didn't come back up. The people who broke the front glass for the counter guns never got out of the showroom.",
